{
 "top": "dsdv_bk_sel_x",
 "why": "PL-BK 10-18: S81-DV bk selector (673.92 x 1296, selv plan) as a landed parent. Children insertion (closed / gated boundary means, TT): rung relays u_rs / u_rn 107-109, glue u_g 265, control u_c ~406 (selc2 gate), quarters ~532 (sq gate): the relays differ by > 150 ps and sit 518 um from the glue, so they get their own regions. The quarters <-> control credit loop (f_c / t_cr out, t_s / t_o back) and the glue -> quarters -> control -> glue (vd) path are ONE strongly connected set: any landing inside it is a cross-region loop (lp.py refuses; the control's SLAT 4 / credit depth would have to be re-scheduled), so quarters + control + glue stay one core region (in-region compensation, see lanes/PL-BK.md).",
